Project: {{config.metadata.name}} ({{stack}} / {{architecture}})
Doc language: {{language}}

Help register a message broker integration (Kafka, RabbitMQ, NATS, ActiveMQ, SQS/SNS, Pub/Sub).
Return ONLY a JSON object — no Markdown fences, no prose.

User input:
"""
{{extra.userDescription}}
"""

Schema:
{
  "name": string,
  "vendor": string,
  "purpose": string,
  "endpoints": [{ "name": string, "protocol": string, "url": string }],
  "slaTargets": { "availability": string, "latencyP95Ms": number },
  "auth": { "mode": string, "secretsRef": string },
  "errorHandling": string,
  "rateLimits": string,
  "observability": string,
  "versioning": string,
  "extra": {
    "flavor": "kafka" | "rabbitmq" | "nats" | "activemq" | "sqs" | "pubsub" | string,
    "topics": string[],
    "exchanges": string[],
    "partitioning": string,
    "ordering": string,
    "delivery": "at-most-once" | "at-least-once" | "exactly-once",
    "deadLetter": string,
    "retentionPolicy": string,
    "consumerGroups": string[],
    "backpressure": string
  }
}

Constraints:
- Do NOT include "id" — INT-NNN is assigned by the tool.
- Specify delivery semantics, partitioning/ordering, and DLQ policy explicitly.

Return JSON only.
